Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   - **Standing binding task (governs everything, from before compaction):** build+flash only via `contest2026_272_tokenwujixian/.claude/skills/bk7258-worktree-build/scripts/full_flow.sh`; test only via `yzhang/testLoop/func-test.sh` + `main_loop.md`/`ui-flow-and-test.md`; verify only unverified items in `verification-record.md`; **do not self-author test scripts** (inline pyserial driving only, no new files).
   - **Security/safety constraints (verbatim, still in force):** `yzhang/cmd_scripts.sh` is mode-600 secret — never dump its values into logs/commits; secrets must be redacted (`contest-log-redact`, must `--verify` print `CLEAN` AND exit 0) before any sync/commit; `set_llm`/`set_dns`/`wapi connect`/`set_volc_key` lines must be piped whole from `cmd_scripts.sh` rather than retyped; **never type bare `reboot` on the board's NSH** (only `reboot bootloader`); never `quit` to exit the agent (hangs; use `restart`/K1/reflash); flash only via `full_flow.sh --flash` in an interactive terminal with device + complete image SHA-256 announced in commentary first.
   - **9-item authoritative task list** (user's own): (1) chat bubble adapts to text length/wraps past 80% width; (2) TTS too quiet/shrill/fast; (3) approval card insufficient info; (4) voice failure feedback must distinguish "didn't speak" from "broken"; (5) notice page truncation/long title overflow/dwell too short; (6) missing glyphs; (7) screen not fully used; (8) font 16→12 px; (9) S2+S3 combo returns to pet screen when no approval pending.
   - **Requests carried into this segment:** TTS speed to 0.5; volume to 40; speaker `zh_female_vv_uranus_bigtts`; fix "卡顿" (stutter) and "读部分词时失声" (dropped words).
   - **New requests in this segment:** (a) "已手动烧录了" — user flashed the new image by hand; (b) "wifi已开" — user turned the hotspot on; (c) **"音色选择有哪些？"** — what voice options exist; (d) **"能不能下载新的？"** — can we get/download new voices.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - BK7258 dual-core AMP; AP NuttX NSH `nsh-ap>` on `/dev/ttyUSB0` (CH340 1a86:7523) at **1,000,000 baud**; CP consoles `/dev/ttyACM0`/`ttyACM1` (CH9102 1a86:55d3, 115200). `vela>` = ai_agent CLI (entered via `ai_agent`); it does not forward NSH commands (no `wapi` there).
   - Volcengine TTS v3: `POST /api/v3/tts/unidirectional`, hosts `openspeech.bytedance.com`, headers `x-api-key` + `X-Api-Resource-Id: seed-tts-2.0`; integer `speech_rate`/`loudness_rate`; chunked newline-delimited JSON; base64 PCM in `data`; last line `code 20000000`.
   - Voice ID family for seed-tts-2.0 is `*_uranus_bigtts`; other resources (seed-tts-1.0 `*_moon_bigtts` etc.) mismatch → error. Official enumeration is `POST /?Action=ListSpeakers&Version=2025-05-20` with `ResourceIDs:["seed-tts-2.0"]`, requires AccessKey signing (not the TTS api key).
   - Measured audio: 16 kHz mono 16-bit PCM = 32,000 B/s; per-segment ceiling `TTS_SEGMENT_MAX 180` UTF-8 bytes.
   - TLS pool: `CONN_POOL_SIZE 2`, `pool_release(slot, host, port, keep)`; batch path already supported keep-alive; **stream path never pooled until this session**; a cold handshake costs ~1-3 s on this SoC.
   - CP↔AP Wi-Fi event path: `cif_get_event_buffer()` uses a **static** pool (`cif_tx_event_buffer[MAX_NUM_CMD_LONG_BUF][...]`, `MAX_NUM_CMD_LONG_BUF 1`, `MAX_NUM_CMD_SHORT_BUF 3`, freed by `cif_free_cmd_buffer` setting `PATTERN_FREE`), so "Failed to allocate memory" = all buffers BUSY, not heap exhaustion.
   - DAC chain: 0..100 → `vol*0x2D/100` gain; 40 → 18/45 (~-8 dB).
   - `/data` is tmpfs → every full flash wipes wapi/LLM/volc config; must re-provision.
   - tmux private socket `/tmp/claude-tmux-sockets/claude.sock`; sessions `flash-bk7258`, `flash`, `bk-flash`, `console`, `ft`, `bk7258-test`.
   - `syslog`-based logging with `TAG` throughout `voice_channel.c`.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **packages/ai_agent/src/infra/vela_tls.c** — the big change of this segment: streaming HTTPS now reuses pooled keep-alive connections (kills the per-sentence TLS handshake gap that caused 卡顿):
     ```c
     int reused = 0;

     if (slot->valid) {
         int stale = (slot->ctx.net.fd < 0);
         if (!stale) {
             unsigned char drain[512];
             struct timeval tv_drain = { .tv_sec = 0, .tv_usec = 10000 };
             struct timeval tv_orig = { .tv_sec = AGENT_LLM_SOCKET_TIMEOUT_SEC, .tv_usec = 0 };
             int dr;
             setsockopt(slot->ctx.net.fd, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO, &tv_drain, sizeof(tv_drain));
             while ((dr = mbedtls_ssl_read(&slot->ctx.ssl, drain, sizeof(drain))) > 0) { }
             setsockopt(slot->ctx.net.fd, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO, &tv_orig, sizeof(tv_orig));
             if (dr == 0 || dr == MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY) stale = 1;
         }
         if (stale) { tls_ctx_free(&slot->ctx); slot->valid = false; }
         else { reused = 1; }  /* tls_ctx_connect must not re-init a live ctx */
     }

     if (!reused && (ret = tls_ctx_connect(&slot->ctx, host, port)) != 0) {
         pool_release(slot, host, port, false); return ret;
     }

     ret = tls_write_request(&slot->ctx, method, host, path, headers, body, body_len);
     if (ret != 0 && reused) {
         syslog(LOG_WARNING, "[%s] stream: pooled connection stale (%d), reconnecting\n", TAG, ret);
         tls_ctx_free(&slot->ctx); slot->valid = false;
         if ((ret = tls_ctx_connect(&slot->ctx, host, port)) == 0)
             ret = tls_write_request(&slot->ctx, method, host, path, headers, body, body_len);
     }
     if (ret != 0) { ...; pool_release(slot, host, port, false); return ret; }
     ```
     Plus framing-completion tracking:
     ```c
     int complete = 0;   /* body consumed to its framing end -> poolable */
     int no_reuse = 0;   /* peer asked for Connection: close           */
     int saw_final = 0;  /* chunked body terminated by the 0 chunk     */
     ...
     { char* conn_hdr = strcasestr(raw, "Connection:");
       if (conn_hdr && conn_hdr < body_start && strcasestr(conn_hdr, "close") != NULL) no_reuse = 1; }
     ...
     if (err == 0 && content_left == 0) complete = 1;      /* non-chunked */
     if (chunk_left <= 0) { saw_final = 1; break; }        /* chunked final */
     if (err == 0 && saw_final) complete = 1;
     ...
     out:
         free(raw); free(acc);
         pool_release(slot, host, port, err == 0 && complete && !no_reuse && http_status > 0);
     ```

   - **packages/ai_agent/src/infra/vela_tls.h** — doc comment replaced: "The connection is never pooled: it lives for this one response." → now explains it is returned to the keep-alive pool when the body was read to its framing end and the peer did not ask for `Connection: close`.

   - **packages/ai_agent/src/voice/voice_channel.c** — diagnostics + write-failure logging:
     ```c
     static struct timespec s_tts_start;
     static int s_tts_first_chunk;
     static int s_tts_chunks;
     static long s_tts_last_chunk_ms;
     static struct timespec s_asr_done_ts;

     static long tts_ms_since_start(void)
     { struct timespec now; clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC,&now);
       return (now.tv_sec-s_tts_start.tv_sec)*1000 + (now.tv_nsec-s_tts_start.tv_nsec)/1000000; }
     ```
     `tts_stream_cb` now logs every chunk with receive offset, gap, length and blocking-write duration, and reports write failures:
     ```c
     long recv_ms = tts_ms_since_start();
     ... struct timespec w0, w1; clock_gettime(&w0);
     int wr = audio_playback_write(pb, pcm_data, pcm_len);
     clock_gettime(&w1);
     long write_ms = ...;
     s_tts_chunks++;
     syslog(LOG_INFO, "[%s] tts chunk %d: +%ldms (gap %ldms) len=%zu write=%ldms\n",
         TAG, s_tts_chunks, recv_ms,
         s_tts_chunks > 1 ? recv_ms - s_tts_last_chunk_ms : 0, pcm_len, write_ms);
     if (wr < 0) syslog(LOG_ERR, "[%s] playback write failed: %d (chunk %zu bytes)\n", TAG, wr, pcm_len);
     s_tts_last_chunk_ms = recv_ms;
     ```
     Speak start resets `s_tts_first_chunk/s_tts_chunks/s_tts_last_chunk_ms`; the segment loop logs `[voice] TTS segment start +%ldms: "%.*s"` (40 bytes) before each `voice_tts_speak_stream(seg, tts_stream_cb, pb)`.

   - **packages/ai_agent/include/agent_config.h** — stale comment corrected to say DAC trimmed to **40** (gain 18/45, ~-8 dB) instead of 50; values unchanged (`SPEAKER "zh_female_vv_uranus_bigtts"`, `SPEED "0.5"`, `VOLUME "1.3"`, `PITCH "0.8"`, `RATIO "1.0"`).

   - **contest2026_272_tokenwujixian/chips/bk7258/include/bk7258_audio.h** — `BK7258_AUDIO_DEFAULT_VOLUME 40` (already applied before this segment).

   - **contest2026_272_tokenwujixian/chips/bk7258/armino_baseline/cp/components/controller_if/cif_mem_mgmt.c** — read-only; proved `cif_get_event_buffer()` scans a static array with 1 long / 3 short buffers, so scan-upload "Failed to allocate memory" is a *pool busy* condition.

   - **packages/ai_agent/src/infra/network_manager.c** — read-only; real-HW `network_wifi_connect()` shells out to `wapi`; `network_wifi_reconnect()` needs saved creds; `net_reconnect` → `network_reconnect()`.

   - **packages/ai_agent/src/channels/nsh_commands.c / cmd_voice.c** — command inventory: `voice_test_speak <text>` → `voice_channel_speak`; `voice_test_tts`, `voice_test_beep`, `set_volc_speaker`, `set_volc_voice`, `net_diag`, `net_reconnect`, `wifi_reconnect`. There is **no `say`** in the AP agent CLI (`say`/`sayc` live in `ui_cp/cp_ui_main.c`).

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **Build raced with edits**: first build exited 0 but may have compiled a pre-fix `vela_tls.c`; reran to confirm `vela_tls.c.o` and `voice_channel.c.o` both rebuilt (log lines `[6/14]`, `[7/14]`).
   - **`-Wsequence-point`**: `++s_tts_chunks` used in the same expression as `s_tts_chunks > 1` at line 648 — fixed by `s_tts_chunks++;` on its own line before the `syslog`.
   - **Lost TLS-connect bug risk**: after enabling reuse, the pre-existing unconditional `tls_ctx_connect()` would re-init a live ctx — fixed with the `reused` flag and a stale-pooled-write retry.
   - **Auto flash injection fails**: `bk_loader` injects `reboot bootloader` at 115200, but the AP console is now 1,000,000 baud, so `do_reset_signal` never reaches NSH; loader window is ~17 s (`LinkCheck Timeout` at +16 s). My 1-Mbaud injection both mid-poll and pre-run failed to engage; board then went silent on all consoles. Fix in practice: user pressed RESET (K1) and flashed manually ("已手动烧录了"). A key nuance I handled: when injecting from a second fd, restore `baudrate = 115200` before closing so the loader's handshake isn't poisoned.
   - **Serial port contention**: a stray inline capture process (`python3 -` reading `/dev/ttyUSB0`, also `p62log.py` on ttyACM2) caused `SerialException: device reports readiness to read but returned no data`; killed via `pkill`/`kill` and `sudo fuser -v /dev/ttyUSB0`.
   - **Wi-Fi scan appeared broken** (`upload_cnt=0`, `get scan result: empty`, `Failed to allocate memory`, netmgr DISCONNECTED): root cause was the **phone hotspot being off**; after the user turned it on ("wifi已开"), the scan returned `upload_cnt=14 ... result=1`, associated `vivo X100 Pro`, `wlan0 10.116.254.233`, `DISCONNECTED -> CONNECTED`.
   - **`say` command unknown** on target (`Unknown command: say`) — correct command is `voice_test_speak`.
   - **New severe issue:** TTS latency exploded on target — first chunk at **+66,391 ms**, chunk gaps ~5-10 s, a fresh TLS handshake to first chunk took **65 s**, while `write=` times stayed 68-250 ms (so the DAC queue was *not* the bottleneck; the data arrival was). Cause not yet identified (candidates: degraded hotspot/cellular uplink, RPMSG/usrsock starvation, CPU1 state).
   - **`/dev/ttyUSB0` disappeared again** at the very end (`FileNotFoundError`), only `ttyACM0/1` (CH9102) enumerating — the CH340 AP console cable is unplugged/unenumerated; needs re-plug (matches the known "TX 掉线 → 拔插 USB" rule).

5. Problem Solving:
   - Implemented and built the keep-alive fix for streaming TTS segments to eliminate per-sentence TLS handshakes (the suspected 卡顿 cause), plus full per-chunk/per-segment instrumentation to attribute future gaps and dropouts.
   - Confirmed the flashed image is the new one (`[voice] TTS segment start +257ms` proves the new code runs) and that the earlier TTS failure was purely "no network".
   - Proved the CP scan-upload failure was environmental (hotspot off), not a code regression.
   - Discovered that the currently observed audio problem is *data starvation* (66 s to first chunk), not buffer underrun from slow writes.
   - Started enumerating this account's usable `*_uranus_bigtts` voices by probing the live v3 endpoint from the host (key pulled from `cmd_scripts.sh` line 56 into an env var, never printed); samples written to `/tmp/tts_voices2/<voice>.wav`, log at `/tmp/voices-probe.log`. Partial results seen: `zh_male_ruyaqingnian_uranus_bigtts`, `zh_male_wennuanahu_uranus_bigtts`, `zh_male_shaonianzixin_uranus_bigtts` all OK (~101 KB PCM each).

6. All user messages:
   - "已手动烧录了"
   - "wifi已开"
   - "音色选择有哪些？"
   - "能不能下载新的？"
   (Earlier, pre-compaction: "已手动烧录了", "读一段长文本，50字左右", "ok,现在语速降下来，不过会有点卡顿、以及在读部分词时失声；而且这个音色我不是很喜欢，你有哪些音色推荐；声音音量调整为40；", "zh_female_vv_uranus_bigtts 用这个吧".)
   Security-relevant constraints restated earlier and still binding: `cmd_scripts.sh` is secret and must never be dumped; secrets redacted with `contest-log-redact` (`--verify` → `CLEAN` + exit 0) before commit; never bare `reboot` on NSH; never `quit` the agent; flash only via `full_flow.sh --flash` with device + full image SHA announced first.

7. Pending Tasks:
   - **Answer the user's voice question**: list the voices this account can actually use (finish reading `/tmp/voices-probe.log`, all 20 candidates), offer WAV samples in `/tmp/tts_voices2/`, and answer 能不能下载新的 (cloud catalog is server-side; switching = change `voice_type`; new/cloned voices require Volc 声音复刻/ICL resource which this key likely lacks — the official enumeration API `ListSpeakers` needs AccessKey signing, not the TTS api key).
   - **Diagnose/fix the 60-second-class TTS latency** now present on target (first chunk 66 s; 65 s handshake-to-first-chunk on segment 2; per-chunk gaps 5-10 s), determine whether it is the hotspot uplink, the AP↔CP network path, or something in the new keep-alive code.
   - **Re-flash the final image once the fix lands** (current flash already carries keep-alive + diagnostics + vv voice + volume 40) and re-provision `/data` after every flash: `wapi` line 33 (nsh-ap>), then `ai_agent`, then `set_dns` 47, `set_llm` 50, `set_volc_key` 56 — all piped whole from `yzhang/cmd_scripts.sh`.
   - Still open from the 9-item list: item 4 (voice failure "didn't speak" vs "broken"), and the stale func-test criterion `8s 后聊天屏让位回宠物` (current policy: no auto-yield; 60 s idle → standby clock).

8. Current Work:
   Immediately before this summary I was doing two things in parallel:
   - A background host-side probe (started with `nohup python3 -` writing `/tmp/voices-probe.log`, WAVs to `/tmp/tts_voices2/`) iterating 20 candidate `*_uranus_bigtts` voice IDs against `https://openspeech.bytedance.com/api/v3/tts/unidirectional` with `X-Api-Resource-Id: seed-tts-2.0`, text `你好，我是你的桌面小助手，很高兴见到你。`, key read from `cmd_scripts.sh` line 56 via env (`KEY="$(sed -n '56p' cmd_scripts.sh | awk '{print $2}')"`), never printed. Last observed lines: `OK zh_male_ruyaqingnian_uranus_bigtts bytes=101514`, `OK zh_male_wennuanahu_uranus_bigtts bytes=101828`, `OK zh_male_shaonianzixin_uranus_bigtts bytes=101512`.
   - Measuring target-side TTS latency with a short text (`voice_test_speak 你好`) after the 48-char run showed first chunk 66,391 ms and 65 s handshake→first-chunk on the second segment — that attempt aborted with `FileNotFoundError: '/dev/ttyUSB0'` because the CH340 AP console cable vanished again (only `/dev/ttyACM0` and `/dev/ttyACM1` present, both 1a86:55d3). Confirmed `ls /dev/ttyUSB*` → "没有那个文件或目录"; `lsusb` shows only the two CH9102 devices and the hub.

9. Optional Next Step:
   Reply to the user's two questions from the completed probe — "音色选择有哪些？" and "能不能下载新的？" — by reading the full `/tmp/voices-probe.log`, listing every voice ID that returned audio (with the Chinese names: vv=Vivi, xiaohe=小何, m191=云舟, taocheng=小天, liufei=刘飞, and whichever of the new candidates worked), pointing at the `/tmp/tts_voices2/*.wav` samples they can audition, and explaining that new voices cannot be "downloaded" — the catalog is server-side and switching is just a `voice_type` change (`set_volc_speaker <id>` at runtime, or the `AGENT_VOICE_DEFAULT_SPEAKER` default at flash time) — while also asking them to re-plug the AP USB console cable so I can continue the latency diagnosis. Direct quotes anchoring this: user "已手动烧录了", "wifi已开", "音色选择有哪些？", "能不能下载新的？"; and my last finding on target was `[voice] TTS first chunk: 66391ms` with `[voice] TTS segment start +125029ms` followed by `vela_tls Handshake OK` and `tts chunk 9: +190215ms (gap 65725ms)`, with `/dev/ttyUSB0` now missing.

